---
title: Red sauce pasta
servings: 6
tags: [italian, beef]
cuisine: italian
time: 1 hour
source: Our own
---

== Sauce ==

Heat the @olive oil{3%tbsp} in a #large pot{} and bloom the
@fennel seed{2%tbsp} ~{1-2%minutes}.

Add the @ground beef{2%lb}, break it into clumps, and brown it deeply
~{10-15%minutes}. Lift it out with a slotted spoon.

Add the @red onion{1}(diced), @fennel{1}(bulb, thinly sliced across),
@jalapeno{1}(minced) and @salt{1%tsp}. Sweat ~{10%minutes}.

Add the @garlic{3%cloves}(minced) and cook ~{2-3%minutes} until soft. Add the
@anchovies{1%tin} and stir until they melt into the vegetables.

Stir in the @ground thyme{2%tsp}, @dried rosemary{2%tsp}(ground) and
@calabrian spaghettata{2%tsp}(or red pepper flakes, to taste).

Add the @tomato paste{6%oz} and cook ~{3%minutes}. Add the
@crushed tomatoes{28%oz}, @dried oregano{2%tsp}, and @salt{} and
@black pepper{} to taste.

Return the beef, add the @bay leaves{2}, and simmer ~{20%minutes} while the
pasta cooks.

== Pasta ==

Bring @water{4%l} to a boil in a #pot{} with @salt{3%tsp}. Cook the
@rigatoni{1%lb} until just short of al dente, about ~{8%minutes}.

== To serve ==

Lift the pasta into the sauce and fold gently so the rigatoni stay whole.

Finish with @ricotta{30%g} and @parmesan{30%g}(freshly grated), and scatter
with @Italian parsley{2%tbsp}(minced).
